    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"The displayed sources show that policy debate is mainly driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_e6c94647c61aec5a\",\"quote\":\"T3. I was a comprehensive school girl who left school at 16, so social mobility is very important to me, and I am pleased to be involved in the new inquiry by the all-party parliamentary group on social mobility into getting people from diverse backgrounds into top professions. Will my hon. Friend tell me what steps the Government are taking to ensure that more people, regardless…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_0733621272cfab2f\",\"quote\":\"I thought I just said that this power is already available and therefore this is a superfluous new clause and we do not need it to give us these powers. I very much doubt Opposition Members will agree with my view that nationalisation of the railways is not the way forward, so stuck as they seem to be in the 1970s, but I hope I may have provided sufficient explanation as to why…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_253838034245d8dd\",\"quote\":\"First, let me be very clear that no such decision has been taken, and we are not contemplating at the moment a commitment of that kind. What I can say is that if we are, in future, to deploy military forces in a combat role into a conflict zone, we would of course, as the Prime Minister has made clear, come to this House first.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"absence of evidence for institutional procedures driving policy debate\",\"mechanism\":\"Misrepresentation of evidence\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim falsely presents the dominant drivers of policy debate, ignoring concerns about social mobility and national security.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The provided evidence focuses on individual concerns, parliamentary procedure, and military deployment, not institutional procedures driving policy. This does not negate the possibility of institutional influence, but it demonstrates the claim's narrow focus and unsupported assertion.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The cited sources demonstrate a range of concerns and debates within the UK Parliament, none of which support the claim that policy debate is *mainly* driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork. The evidence highlights diverse issues, including social mobility, railway nationalization, and military deployment, indicating a broader range of influences.\"}",
    "done": true,
    "done_reason": "stop",
